+# Start here — Claude takeover
+
+Updated November 9, 2026.
+
+The founder wants one complete design pass with the refinement and restraint of https://www.namuai-lab.com/, using Vocalis's own business, mint/navy identity, media and approved claims. The prior version was cleaner but still looked too much like a generic software template.
+
+**Paste or read `CLAUDE_REFINEMENT_PROMPT.md` as the implementation brief.** It includes copy-editing rules, specific visual compositions, scope, approved claims, mobile requirements and acceptance criteria. Read `DESIGN_REVIEW.md` for the evidence and existing fixes.
+
+Worktree: `/Users/somesh/Desktop/websites/home-redesign` (branch `redesign/vocalis-2026`). The sibling `home` checkout is historical and stores the handoff package. Preserve existing staged/unstaged work. The review refinement was prepared separately before application; the change manifest and verification report identify its files.
+
+Priorities, in order:
+
+1. Preserve the tested mobile/stability fixes and restored founder-approved claims.
+2. Give the hero and main demo the visual confidence of Namu; use the seven composition requirements in the prompt.
+3. Finish distinct Home, Product, Workflows, Security and About pages. Pricing is outside the refinement scope.
+4. Keep the definition prominent. Refine the bounded draggable footer without harming scrolling, accessibility or performance.
+5. Edit every visible sentence for a real clinic audience, keeping the actual capabilities and meaning.
+6. Review the entire result at desktop and phone sizes, run the build/tests and report actual measured outcomes.
+
+Evidence and references live in `review-evidence/` and `references/`. The file paths for pitch slides, dashboard and video source are in the prompt and source audit. No production deployment has been performed. A device QA requirement is not permission to claim a physical iPhone was tested.
